# Targets to delete from $HOME on apply.
#
# Ghostty loads ~/.config/ghostty/config AND the macOS-native
# ~/Library/Application Support/com.mitchellh.ghostty/config, then merges them.
# Keeping both duplicated every list-valued key — `ghostty +show-config` showed
# font-family twice — and let the two copies drift, so the split-navigation
# keybinds only ever reached one of them. ~/.config/ghostty/config is the single
# source now; this drops the leftover copy.
Library/Application Support/com.mitchellh.ghostty/config

# espanso, replaced by vicinae's built-in snippets. Dropping the source files
# alone would leave both of these behind, since chezmoi does not delete what it
# merely stopped managing. The second is the symlink that pointed at the first.
.config/espanso
Library/Application Support/espanso

# The work-only pi package, on private machines. .chezmoiignore stops chezmoi
# managing it, but an earlier apply had already deployed it — and chezmoi never
# deletes what it merely stopped managing.
{{ if not .isWorkComputer }}
.pi/agent/packages/terraform-workflow
{{ end }}

# Pre-mise fish snippets that were never managed here. golang.fish pinned
# GOROOT to /opt/homebrew/opt/go/libexec — a Homebrew go that no longer exists
# — so whenever mise's own GOROOT export was absent (which is exactly what
# happens while a go install is failing) every `go` invocation died with
# "cannot find GOROOT directory", including the version check mise runs after
# unpacking a new toolchain. Never set GOROOT/GOPATH by hand with mise: it
# exports both for the active version, and MISE_GO_SET_GOBIN (shell.yaml) puts
# `go install` binaries on PATH. go.fish set that same variable a second time.
.config/fish/conf.d/golang.fish
.config/fish/conf.d/go.fish

# Two more of the same vintage. node.fish prepended $HOME/.n/bin (the `n`
# version manager, long gone — the directory does not exist) *ahead* of
# everything, which is precisely the position mise's shims need; had `n` ever
# come back it would have silently outranked the pinned node. rust.fish added
# $HOME/.cargo/bin, which shell.yaml's universal path tier already owns.
.config/fish/conf.d/node.fish
.config/fish/conf.d/rust.fish
